<title>USA: Mediation urged in American talks.</title>
<headline>Mediation urged in American talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of the Senate Aviation subcommittee Friday urged President Clinton to help mediate a settlement in the American Airlines labor dispute to avert a strike scheduled for Feb. 15.</p>
<p>Sen. Slade Gorton, R-Washington, in a letter signed by 16 other senators, urged Clinton to use the powers and persuasions of his office, along with the National Mediation Board, to help the airline and its pilots reach a settlement. The White House on Friday said it was ready to help if the parties asked for assistance.</p>
</text>
